msgstr ""

#: source/development/debugging.md:3
msgid ""
"This section shows how to build and debug Nix with debug symbols enabled."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/debugging.md:5
msgid ""
"Additionally, see [Testing Nix](./testing.md) for further instructions on "
"how to debug Nix in the context of a unit test or functional test."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/debugging.md:7
msgid "Building Nix with Debug Symbols"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/debugging.md:9
msgid ""
"In the development shell, `mesonBuildType` is set automatically to "
"`debugoptimized`. This builds Nix with debug symbols, which are essential "
"for effective debugging."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/debugging.md:11
msgid "It is also possible to build without optimization for faster build:"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/debugging.md:18
msgid ""
"(The first line is needed because `fortify` hardening requires at least some "
"optimization.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/debugging.md:20
msgid "Building Nix with sanitizers"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/debugging.md:22
msgid ""
"Nix can be built with [Address](https://clang.llvm.org/docs/AddressSanitizer."
"html) and [UB](https://clang.llvm.org/docs/UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer.html) "
"sanitizers using LLVM or GCC. This is useful when debugging memory "
"corruption issues."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/debugging.md:26
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"[nix-shell]$ export mesonBuildType=debugoptimized\n"
"[nix-shell]$ appendToVar mesonFlags \"-Dlibexpr:gc=disabled\" # Disable "
"Boehm\n"
"[nix-shell]$ appendToVar mesonFlags \"-Db_sanitize=address,undefined\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

